    883:| §P.P2 batched π_h(x) on h, slot 1 — does the parallel-h Eratosthenes sieve produce per-h amortised polylog cost as M = #h grows, or does it bottom out at Θ(x/log x) (P1-shape)? | EXPERIMENT (B-NEGATIVE on EXACT regime; B-POSITIVE on APPROXIMATE regime — Thread-7-shape transposed to h-axis) | E (E1.5 + S224 + S231 + S240..S244 — per-h amortised cost = Θ(x/log x) for batched-sieve; HL polylog-per-h with √x error matches Hardy-Littlewood prediction) | Thread 8 commit step 1/4 (S418). Built `experiments/analytic/batched_pi_h/slot1_baseline.py` (~280 lines) implementing three estimators of π_h(x) := #{p prime, p ≤ x : p+h prime} for h ∈ {2, 4, ..., H}: M1 BATCHED SIEVE (sieve [1, x+H] once, for each prime p ≤ x test all H/2 candidates p+h), M2 PER-h SIEVE (single-h timing × M for prediction), M3 HARDY-LITTLEWOOD APPROX (HL_h(x) = S_h · li_2(x), S_h = 2 C_2 Π_{p|h, p odd} (p−1)/(p−2), li_2 via scipy.integrate.quad). **Three-anchor table** at x = 10⁵ / 10⁶ / 10⁷ with H = ⌊log²x⌋ even-rounded capped at 200, M = 66 / 95 / 100: T_batched = 0.041 / 0.438 / 3.893 s ⇒ per-h amort = 0.62 / 4.61 / 38.9 ms. M1/M2 batched-vs-per-h speedup at x = 10⁵, 10⁶: 6.71×, 8.85× — **bounded constant, not growing with M**. Per-h amort ratio across decades: 7.7×, 8.5× ≈ π(x) ratios 8.18×, 8.47× — **per-h amortised cost is Θ(π(x)) = Θ(x/log x), NOT polylog**. **H-sweep at x = 10⁶** with H ∈ {20, 50, 100, 200, 400}, M ∈ {10, 25, 50, 100, 200}: per-h amortised = 8.7 → 6.0 → 5.0 → 4.5 → 4.3 ms — clear floor at ~4 ms (set by per-prime per-h test cost: π(10⁶) · 50 ns ≈ 4 ms). **Per-h cost is M-INDEPENDENT for M ≥ 50.** **HL approximation per-h cost** = 0.62 / 1.23 / 0.68 µs — five orders of magnitude faster than batched-sieve, flat in x and M (polylog shape). **HL approximation accuracy**: mean |π_h − HL_h|/√x ≤ 0.10, max ≤ 0.25 across all 261 (x, H, h) cells; matches Hardy-Littlewood's O(√x) conjectural bound. **Structural dichotomy** (the slot's main result): EXACT regime per-h cost = Θ(x/log x) with zero error (matches P1 / Thread 6 negative shape on the h-axis); APPROXIMATE regime per-h cost = Θ(polylog x) with ≤ 0.25 √x worst error (matches P3 / Thread 7 positive shape on the h-axis). **P2 is Thread-7 (P3) shape, NOT Thread-5 (S224) shape**: the cross-h amortisation in EXACT regime gives only a constant sieve-sharing factor (the h-axis is not a "correlation-of-x" axis in the relevant sense). **What this rules out**: (i) batched-sieve algorithm achieving o(x/log x) per-h amortised for any unbounded M family — directly tested at M ∈ {10..200} and ruled out; (ii) Thread-5-style cross-h correlation amortisation matching the 33× S224 speedup — does not materialise; (iii) the original P2 entry's "shared-h-singular-series structure" being interpreted as exact-cost amortisation — the shared structure helps only the polylog HL approximation, not the EXACT count. **What this does NOT close**: (i) non-sieve algorithms (GPY-weight / Maynard) for batched EXACT π_h — outside slot-1 scope; (ii) quantum batched (P9 shape); (iii) the precise named-exponent error bound for HL approximation — slot 2/3/4 candidate; (iv) the Q-truncation tradeoff for S_Q(h) → S_h — slot 3 candidate. **Pivoted A-grade target for slots 2-4**: precise named-exponent error bound for HL approximation, analogue of Thread 7 Corollary B but for π_h(x). **Cross-domain ingredient**: Hardy-Littlewood k-tuple conjecture (1923) + singular series. CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md status unchanged (singular series already USED-E in `sanity_singular_series.py`). **Cites** E1.5 (per-h sample-complexity argument), E6.x (sieve hierarchy primitive), S224 (Correlation Dichotomy template — NOT replicated for h-axis), S231 (Thread 6 P1 wrap — negative shape this slot matches in EXACT regime), S240-S244 (Thread 7 P3 — positive shape this slot matches in APPROX regime). See `experiments/analytic/batched_pi_h/{slot1_baseline.py, slot1_baseline_results.md, slot1_raw.tsv, slot1_samples.tsv}`, `archive/sessions/session418_commit_p2_baseline.md`. | 418 |
    885:| §P.P2 batched π_h(x) on h, slot 2 — does the within-window cross-x ensemble of HL residuals r_h(x) = π_h(x) − S_h·li_2(x) at fixed (anchor, h) follow a half-Gaussian shape (Thread 7 slot 2 transposition); is there a stable F_GUE-like factor σ_eff/σ_pred? | EXPERIMENT (B-MIXED: cross-x within-window FAILS half-Gaussian KS due to random-walk-like correlation; cross-h at fixed x PASSES with median KS p ≈ 0.7-0.8; σ-suppression ratio in [0.36, 0.70] but NOT decade-stable like Thread 7's F_GUE = 0.755) | E (E1.5 + S195 + S224 + S240..S244 + S418 — methodological finding identifies cross-h as the natural ensemble for HL residual analysis; refines slot-1 dichotomy into ensemble-aware form) | Thread 8 commit step 2/4 (S419). Built `experiments/analytic/batched_pi_h/slot2_multisample.py` (~340 lines): batched-sieve via numpy AND-shift cumsum (memory-efficient; 720 rows in 21s total wall time). Three anchors x ∈ {10⁶, 10⁷, 10⁸} × N=30 log-uniform x_j in quarter-decade [x_anchor, x_anchor·10^{0.25}] × 8 representative h ∈ {2, 6, 14, 22, 30, 42, 90, 198} (S_h ∈ [1.32, 4.0]). Three statistical aggregates: (A) per-(anchor, h) cross-x KS (24 cells, N=30 each); (B) per-(anchor, x_j) cross-h KS (90 cells, N=8 each); (C) pooled per-anchor (N=240 each). **Headline finding**: cross-x at fixed (anchor, h) FAILS half-Gaussian KS — median p_eff = 0.033, only 8/24 cells with p > 0.1. Cells that fail show median/σ_eff ≈ mean/σ_eff ≈ 0.95 (theoretical half-Gaussian = 0.6745/0.7979) — clustered |r| values, not Gaussian-tailed. Within-window range diagnostic: (max|r| − min|r|)/σ_eff has mean ≈ 1.5 across cells; residuals drift but don't decohere. **Structural diagnosis**: HL_h(x) = S_h · li_2(x) is analytic-smooth, π_h(x) is step; the residual is a slowly-varying random-walk in x (drift O(σ_eff) within quarter-decade, no oscillation), unlike Thread 7's zero-truncation residual which oscillates with wavelength ~1/log x. Cross-x sampling within a small log-window does NOT give iid samples for HL residuals. **Cross-h at fixed (anchor, x_j) PASSES half-Gaussian KS**: median p_eff = 0.840 / 0.698 / 0.804 at anchors 10⁶/10⁷/10⁸; **all 90/90 cells with p > 0.1**. The cross-h ensemble is the natural sampling for HL residual shape analysis. **σ-suppression ratio σ_eff/σ_pred_pois = 0.36-0.70** across 24 (anchor, h) cells, where σ_pred_pois = √(S_h·li_2(x)) is the HL random-residual Poisson prediction. Empirical RMS is consistently SMALLER than Poisson — analogue of Thread 7's GUE pair-correlation suppression (correlations among primes via singular series itself reduce the variance below random-residual). NOT decade-stable: 0.50 → 0.70 → 0.41 across 10⁶/10⁷/10⁸; the 10⁷ bump driven by anomaly cell (10⁷, h=6) cousin-prime σ_eff/σ_pois = 1.64 (signed range = 481, persistent large residual episode). Excluding h=6: ratio narrows to ~0.36-0.43, still mildly drifting with x. **Pooled per-anchor (N=240) KS**: borderline at 10⁶ (p=0.082), reject at 10⁷ (p<0.001, h=6 outlier), borderline at 10⁸ (p=0.217). Half-Gaussian shape holds at the cell level but pooled hides the anomaly. **What this rules out**: (i) the original Thread-7-direct-transposition hypothesis "HL has stable F_GUE-like σ_eff/σ_pred ≈ 0.74 across decades" — directly tested, ratio drifts in [0.36, 0.70]; (ii) cross-x sampling within quarter-decade as a fair iid ensemble for HL residual statistics — methodologically rejected. **What this does NOT close**: (i) cross-h ensemble at fixed x as a path to a precise σ-formula for HL — slot 2 demonstrates shape but does not derive σ_eff(x, h) closed form; (ii) Q-truncated singular series cost-vs-error tradeoff — slot 3; (iii) anchor extension to 10⁹/10¹⁰ to test whether σ_eff/σ_pois stabilises — slot 3 side measurement; (iv) named-exponent error bound for polylog HL evaluator — slot 3-4 wrap. **Methodological warning** (preserved for slot 3+ design): within-window cross-x sampling is misleading for HL residual analysis; use cross-h at fixed x. **Cross-domain ingredient**: Hardy-Littlewood random-residual heuristic (predicted Poisson scale √(S_h · li_2(x))) plus Kolmogorov-Smirnov half-Gaussian goodness-of-fit (signal-processing standard). CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md unchanged. **Cites** E1.5 (per-query bit content), S195 (variance machinery transposed to h-axis), S224 (Correlation Dichotomy reference), S418 (slot-1 dichotomy this slot extends), S240-S244 (Thread 7 P3 — ensemble-shape contrast). See `experiments/analytic/batched_pi_h/{slot2_multisample.py, slot2_multisample_results.md, slot2_data.csv, slot2_summary.csv, slot2_cross_h.csv, slot2_pooled.csv, slot2_run.log}`, `archive/sessions/session419_commit_p2_multisample.md`. | 419 |
