Session 420 (Thread 8 / P2 slot 3 of 4) complete, **B-grade**.

**Headline:** named-exponent variance decomposition for the Q-truncated HL approximation HL_Q(h, x) = S_Q(h)·li_2(x):

   σ²_HL_Q(x, h-ensemble) = σ²_∞(x) + (1/N)·Σ_{h: max_p>Q} (ε_Q(h)·li_2(x))²

Empirically verified at 16 (anchor, x_j, Q) cells across two decades within 5–25% of σ_emp. **Knee scaling Q\* ≈ √x/log x** confirmed at both anchors (knee_max_p = 199 at 10⁷ vs predicted 196; 599–1009 at 10⁸ vs predicted 543). Sharp half-Gaussian shape transition Q=100 → Q=200 (KS median p 0.0015 → 0.96). Q-truncation provides no asymptotic cost saving in the original P2 polylog regime — knee Q\* is *algebraic* in x, not polylog.

**Slot 4 (FINAL) target**: theoretical wrap, rigorising the variance decomposition under cross-h Hardy-Littlewood random-residual hypothesis via Goldston-Montgomery 1987 bilinear-form adaptation. Conditional theorem analogue of S244 Corollary B for π_h batches. `.run_state` set to 422.
